 466:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** 
 467:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** /*********************************************************************
 468:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *
 469:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *       SEGGER_RTT_printf
 470:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *
 471:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *  Function description
 472:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *    Stores a formatted string in SEGGER RTT control block.
 473:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *    This data is read by the host.
 474:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *
 475:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *  Parameters
 476:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *    BufferIndex  Index of "Up"-buffer to be used. (e.g. 0 for "Terminal")
 477:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *    sFormat      Pointer to format string, followed by the arguments for conversion
 478:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *
 479:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *  Return values
 480:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *    >= 0:  Number of bytes which have been stored in the "Up"-buffer.
 481:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *     < 0:  Error
 482:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *
 483:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *  Notes
 484:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *    (1) Conversion specifications have following syntax:
ARM GAS  /var/folders/yl/_q9l42k90g1g4mdhbs226msm0000gn/T//ccDWgBb0.s 			page 31


 485:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          %[flags][FieldWidth][.Precision]ConversionSpecifier
 486:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *    (2) Supported flags:
 487:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          -: Left justify within the field width
 488:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          +: Always print sign extension for signed conversions
 489:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          0: Pad with 0 instead of spaces. Ignored when using '-'-flag or precision
 490:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *        Supported conversion specifiers:
 491:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          c: Print the argument as one char
 492:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          d: Print the argument as a signed integer
 493:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          u: Print the argument as an unsigned integer
 494:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          x: Print the argument as an hexadecimal integer
 495:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          s: Print the string pointed to by the argument
 496:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          p: Print the argument as an 8-digit hexadecimal integer. (Argument shall be a pointer to
 497:./SystemView/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** */
